-- ============================================================================
-- PD1 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Nodal Analysis & Well Performance, intermediate
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE OUTFLOW. What the tubing will take. It is the half
-- of the problem the engine deliberately does NOT own, and the tier is built
-- around that fact.
--
-- THE CURVE IS J SHAPED BECAUSE TWO TERMS PULL OPPOSITE WAYS. A column
-- lightens as rate rises and friction grows as the square of rate, so the
-- required bottomhole pressure falls, reaches a minimum, and then rises. Which
-- SIDE of that minimum a well sits on is what the entire Expert tier turns on,
-- so this tier has to leave the reader able to locate it and to distrust the
-- location. The minimum is a REDUCTION OVER SAMPLED ROWS, not an analytic
-- one: near a minimum the pressure is flat, so the rate it reports is the
-- least reliable feature of the curve while the pressure there is very nearly
-- exact. On the capstone's 49 point curve the minimum sits at 1285.2338 stb/d
-- and 2849.6728 psia, and the operating point sits 386.2613 stb/d to the LEFT
-- of it and 96.6563 psi above it.
--
-- THE ENGINE INJECTS THE OUTFLOW AND NEVER CHECKS IT. The module has no
-- reservoir in it, so it cannot say whether the well flows, and it validates
-- nothing about the curve it is handed. A curve computed on the wrong pressure
-- basis or the wrong flow regime is solved exactly as confidently as a correct
-- one, and two consumers can disagree about one well while both stay
-- internally consistent.
--
-- THE ONE COLUMN IT DOES BUILD, AND THE RECORDED DEFECT IN IT.
-- `cullenderSmithBhp` defaults to `steps: 2`, which IS the published
-- two-station method. Its truncation is a FRICTION problem and not a gravity
-- one, and the capstone's own gas column proves it on one string: at two steps
-- a gravity only column is off by -0.136426 psi, while the same column carrying
-- 9.6 MMscf/d is off by -4.506808 psi. Thirty three times the error from the
-- same truncation, because the integrand only changes character once friction
-- is comparable to gravity, and two stations have nothing to bend with.
-- RAISING THAT DEFAULT IS AN OWNER DECISION, NOT A FIX: it would move a
-- displayed bottomhole pressure in Nodal Analysis Studio. The capstone
-- therefore FIXES the step count at twenty in its stated conditions and says
-- why, so that the step count is part of the question rather than part of the
-- answer key.
--
-- THE CAPSTONE'S OUTFLOW IS A WELL THAT CANNOT START ITSELF. Both ends of the
-- tubing curve, 5046.5651 psia at the low rate end and 5277.4113 psia at the
-- open flow end, stand ABOVE the reservoir pressure of 3450 psia. A learner
-- who reports a low rate end below reservoir pressure has evaluated the
-- gravity term in the wrong place, and the free check catches it.
-- ============================================================================

values ('nodal', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-column-pushes-back","title":"The Column Pushes Back","lesson_keys":["l01-what-outflow-means","l02-the-three-pressure-losses","l03-why-the-engine-injects-it","l04-what-a-tubing-curve-is"]},{"key":"m02-the-j-shape","title":"The J Shape","lesson_keys":["l01-two-terms-pulling-opposite-ways","l02-the-gravity-limb","l03-the-friction-limb","l04-the-minimum","l05-what-the-shape-tells-a-designer"]},{"key":"m03-what-moves-the-curve","title":"What Moves the Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-wellhead-pressure","l02-tubing-size","l03-water-cut-and-density","l04-lifting-gas","l05-one-change-two-effects"]},{"key":"m04-the-gas-column","title":"The Gas Column","lesson_keys":["l01-why-dry-gas-is-the-one-built-in","l02-cullender-and-smith","l03-the-static-gradient","l04-steps-and-truncation"]},{"key":"m05-the-injection-pressure","title":"The Injection Pressure","lesson_keys":["l01-what-a-valve-needs","l02-annulus-versus-tubing","l03-reading-a-depth","l04-average-t-and-z-as-a-check","l05-what-the-column-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
